# Atlas: only the LARGE reproducible artifacts stay out of Git.
#
#   atlas/raw/                      219 MB of sha256-pinned upstream downloads (`npm run atlas:fetch`)
#   shapes-corridor.geojson          24.6 MB of corridor geometry, rebuilt by `npm run atlas:import`
#
# Everything else the pipeline derives is committed on purpose, so a fresh clone can serve and validate
# the corpus without network access to Zenodo or Natural Earth: entities/assertions/anomalies JSON and
# the 1.3 MB focus-tier shapes are about 2.3 MB in total. `npm run atlas:build` regenerates all of it
# from the pinned sources, and `npm run atlas:validate` proves it is internally consistent.
#
# There is deliberately no `public/atlas/tiles` entry: vector tiling was evaluated and rejected. The
# worst single-year payload in the pilot corridor is 12 shapes and about 0.36 MB, which does not
# justify a tile server, so no such directory should ever exist.
atlas/data/pilot/cliopatria/shapes-corridor.geojson
